            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "The following code:\n\n```\ncon1 <- textConnection(\"out\", \"w\")\ncat(\"a\", file = con1)                # incomplete line: kept in C buffer, 'out' not yet locked\ncon2 <- textConnection(\"out\", \"w\")   # rebinds 'out'; con1's character vector is now unreferenced\ngc()                                 # frees it, but con1 still points to it\nclose(con1)                          # outtext_close() uses the freed STRSXP\n```\n\nResulted in this output (R-devel built with `--enable-strict-barrier`):\n\n```\nError in close.connection(con1) :\n  unprotected object (0x52500261ba70) encountered (was STRSXP)\nCalls: close -> close.connection\nExecution halted\n```\n\nOn a stock R 4.6.1 (Docker `r-base:latest`) the freed node gets reused, and the same code (with some allocation between `gc()` and `close()`) gives errors such as\n\n```\nError in close.connection(con1) :\n  SET_STRING_ELT() can only be applied to a 'character vector', not a 'pairlist'\n```\n\nor, under `gctorture(TRUE)`, `cannot set length of non-(vector or list)`.\n\nFor an output text connection with a named `object`, `Routtextconn->data` (connections.c) is protected only by the binding of that name in the target environment. `R_PreserveObject()` is used only when `object = NULL`. Anything that drops the binding leaves `data` dangling. `outtext_close()` and `text_vfprintf()` then call `xlengthgets(this->data, ...)` on a freed node. The same happens when `close()` is never called and the connection's finalizer runs `outtext_close()` during `gc()`. Other ways to trigger it:\n\n```\ncon <- textConnection(\"out\", \"w\"); rm(out); gc(); cat(\"x\\n\", file = con)\n```\n\nThis one fails even after a complete line has been written, so the binding is locked (`bindingIsLocked(\"out\", globalenv())` is `TRUE`), because `rm()` still removes it. Also, in `\"w\"` mode `outtext_init()` does not lock the binding at creation, although `?textConnection` says the binding is locked until `close`. It is only locked after the first complete line in `text_vfprintf()`, which is what lets a second `textConnection(\"out\", \"w\")` silently replace it.\n\nA possible fix is to preserve `this->data` (`R_PreserveObject`/`R_ReleaseObject`) whether or not `namesymbol` is set, as is already done for `object = NULL`.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n```\nRscript --vanilla ./min.R\n```\n\nCommit:\n```\ncf22bdfad2161aa9b2f8e79b786b68588936d722 (R-devel r90659, 2026-10-10); outtext_init() is unchanged in trunk as of r90686 (2026-10-16)\n```\n\nBuild configuration:\n```\n../configure CC=\"clang-18 -fsanitize=address -fno-omit-frame-pointer\" CXX=\"clang++-18 -fsanitize=address -fno-omit-frame-pointer\" \\\n  FC=gfortran F77=gfortran CFLAGS=\"-O1 -g\" CXXFLAGS=\"-O1 -g\" \\\n  --enable-strict-barrier --with-recommended-packages=no \\\n  --with-x=no --with-tcltk=no --with-cairo=no --with-aqua=no \\\n  --disable-java --disable-nls --disable-openmp\n```\n\nOperating System:\n```\nUbuntu 24.04.4 LTS (Docker), x86_64; also observed on Docker r-base:latest (R 4.6.1)\n```",
            "bug_id": 19228
          },
          {
