            "bug_id": 19228,
            "text": "Created attachment 3947\npatch: anchor the vector behind an output textConnection in OutTextData, lock \"w\" binding at creation\n\nPatch attached (against r90759). Rather than adding R_PreserveObject()\ncalls, it anchors the current vector in OutTextData, the preserved\nper-connection root that already holds the target environment, as\nlist(env, data). That also drops the per-line R_PreserveObject() /\nR_ReleaseObject() the object = NULL path (capture.output) has always\ndone. It also locks the binding at creation in \"w\" mode, as \"a\" mode\ndoes and ?textConnection describes, so a second \"w\" connection on an\nopen name is an error rather than orphaning the first; base R's own\nuses are unaffected. That part can be dropped if unwanted.\n\nIncludes a regression test that fails on unpatched trunk with the\nSET_STRING_ELT() error from the report. Checked on an\n--enable-strict-barrier build.\n\nAlso at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/401 with CI results.",
            "count": 2,
